course: dictionary
lesson: 14068
title: Matting: a floor cover or tangled fur
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Matting can mean two different things, so the context tells you which one. Matting is a material, such as rubber, rope, straw or plastic, that covers a floor. «The gym has thick rubber matting under the bars, so a fall hurts less.» The clues are gym, floor and falls, so matting is the cover on the ground.
explain: Matting can also describe hair or fur that has tangled into thick knots. «The dog's fur had matting behind its ears.» The clue is fur, and the word knots would fit well here. Ask: is this about a floor or about hair? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Matting is a material used to cover floors, often sold in large rolls.
fact: Matting can be made from rubber, rope, straw or plastic.
fact: «Matting» in hair or fur means hair that has tangled into thick knots.
fact: Non-slip matting stops people from slipping, for example in bathrooms.
fact: Pet owners brush dogs and cats to stop matting.
exercise: «The swing has rubber matting underneath, so falls hurt less.» What is matting here? | A game played in the gym | * A material that covers the ground | A kind of swing | A tangled knot of hair
exercise: «Brush the cat every day to stop matting.» What does matting mean here? | A soft toy for the cat | A sort of bath | * Hair that has tangled into thick knots | A type of cat food
exercise: Ella asks, «Why is there non-slip matting in the bathroom?» Which answer fits best? | To make the room smell nice | To keep the floor warm | * To stop people from slipping | To hold up the towels
test: «Rolls of plastic matting covered the gym floor.» What is the matting? | A pile of hairy blankets | Warm bread | A ball game | * A material that covers a floor
test: «The dog's coat had matting under its collar.» What does matting mean here? | A kind of dog lead | A new dog collar | A brush sold in shops | * Thick tangled knots of fur
exam: Which sentence uses matting to mean tangled fur? | «The floor had new matting laid across it.» | * «The cat's fur had hard matting on its back.» | «The rubber matting was soft and springy.»
